#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3fcc3-fa0d-5f01-ba15-7551732faeaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561210} {:answer/id #uuid "52d1d98a-2227-583b-995d-2d9f0f210a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561211} {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656364}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256} :answer-field/id #uuid "43673130-deba-5b98-8ce2-b4ee4ed0101a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7e53da6-3b28-54ab-be32-bc2afa7301df" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x + y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x + 3y &{}={}& 3\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + y &=-1 \\\\ -12x + 3y &= 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &= 3 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(-5x - 1\\right) &= 3 \\\\\n-12x - 15x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."}]}
